# Drafted by Gemini (R19 isolde), edited. Isolde the grim speaks in Narrator lines only.

~ door
set isolde_met
set isolde_alive
Narrator: A spectral black hound stands braced against the seam of the great iron doors, hackles raised and bright white eyes unblinking. Between her jaws she grips the brass ring of a hooded lantern.
* Offer her a hand -> door_hand
* [Animal Handling DC 12] Calm her -> door_calm | door_hand
* Leave her to her work -> END

~ door_hand
approve lucan_houndstooth +2 rook_coldwake +1: You offered a steady hand to the spectral hound guarding the door
Narrator: The hound sniffs your outstretched knuckles and gives your skin one cool, rough lick before turning back to watch the iron seam.
-> END

~ door_calm
Narrator: The bristle along the hound's dark spine smooths flat, and she watches you with the quiet steadiness of a sentry who knows a friend.
-> END

~ fades
set isolde_faded
set isolde_alive = 0
cutscene mm_isolde_fades
Narrator: Left too long at her post, Isolde thins like smoke until her hooded lantern gutters out and vanishes. Grave mist immediately hisses through the unguarded iron seam.
set mm_isolde_lurkers
-> END

~ farewell
set mm_isolde_farewelled
cutscene mm_isolde_farewell
Narrator: Under the steady glow of the six burning sconces, Isolde rises from the threshold and shakes the damp from her coat. She turns toward the carved stones of the Shadestone Clan and looks back once, waiting for you to follow.
-> END
